   Prop 6 hypothesis edge cases:
      r/n <= r/(b+r+1) whenever n>=b+r+1 : trivially true; at r=0 both are 0.
      the level-(r-1),b+1 hypothesis needs n >= (b+1)+(r-1)+1 = b+r+1  -> SAME range: OK
      (n-a-1-b-r)/n in [0,1] over every valid (n,a,b,r) with n>=b+r+1 : True
      at a = n-b-r-1 (h_r's own top boundary) it is EXACTLY 0, which is what
      makes the out-of-domain reference g_r(b+r+1,b+1) harmless (issue I-2).

